    "q-162945": {
      "dom_id": "step-q162945",
      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "Consider the function $f:{R}^{2}\\to R,$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)={x}^{2}+y,\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf the tangent to $f$ at $a=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ is given by\n\n$$\nz-∗=[\\begin{aligned}∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}]([\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}])\n$$\n\nwhat is the sum of the missing values?",
      "worked_solution": "Suppose a transformation $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{m}$ is defined by \n\n$$\nf:[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{f}_{1}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ {f}_{2}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {f}_{m}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${f}_{1},{f}_{2},…,{f}_{m}$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $f$ is differentiable at $x,$ then the total derivative of $f$ at $x,$ denoted ${f}^{′}(x),$ is given by the $m\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+y)=2x,\\, & \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+y)=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}2x & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f$ and its derivative at $x=a=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],$ we have\n\n$$\nf(a)=0,\\,{f}^{′}(a)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe tangent to $f$ at $x=a$ is given by\n\n$$\nz-f(a)={f}^{′}(a)(x-a).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $f(a),$ ${f}^{′}(a),$ and $a$ in the equation above, we obtain\n\n$$\nz-0=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1\\end{aligned}]([\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the missing values is\n\n$$\n0+2+1=3.\n$$",
